 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ to compute the center of mass and covariance matrix. Eigenvalue decomposition of a $3 \times 3$ matrix is $O(1)$ (constant time, typically involving solving a cubic equation or iterative methods). Total time is linear in the number of vertices [G].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ to store the vertices and the centered vertices. The covariance matrix and eigenpairs are $O(1)$ [G].
-*   **Strengths:** Provides a canonical orientation for meshes based on their shape, which is robust to translation. It is deterministic for a given mesh [G].
-*   **Limitations:** Sensitive to the distribution of vertices; noise can affect the principal axes. It does not account for semantic orientation (e.g., "up" direction) unless constrained [G].
